Just about any Promise card works fine... Its not only faster than the
standard Alpha IDE, but supports UDMA w/sync burst as well. I get upwards of
25MBs transfer rates with mine [Kernel-2.6.13.4].

You should be able to do like I did...

Compile your kernel with Promise Card support
Place your kernel on the boot drive partitioned /boot
Have your UDMA drive, one on the Promise card, mounted as /

It will work like a top. I used a el'cheapo 50MB boot drive and 2 36GB
drives are my main drives

Will L G

